{
  "id": "vuvuzela_part1",
  "title": "Vuvuzela Saves the Day! Part 1",
  "audioFile": "audio.mp3",
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "text": "Lerato lived in a small village in South Africa."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "text": "One day, her father gave her a vuvuzela."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "text": "\"It makes a loud sound like an elephant.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "text": "\"People blow it at soccer matches,\" he said."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "text": "Lerato blew the vuvuzela, but no sound came out."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "text": "She felt sad."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "text": "\"Keep practicing!\" Lerato's father said."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "text": "Later, the people in the village went to get water."
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "text": "Suddenly, Lerato saw a tall man in her neighbor's house."
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "text": "He was stealing money!"
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "text": "He was a thief!"
    },
    {
      "id": "12",
      "text": "Lerato was scared."
    },
    {
      "id": "13",
      "text": "She looked for an adult."
    },
    {
      "id": "14",
      "text": "But no one was there."
    },
    {
      "id": "15",
      "text": "\"I must call the villagers back!\" Lerato thought."
    },
    {
      "id": "16",
      "text": "\"But my voice is too soft!\""
    },
    {
      "id": "17",
      "text": "Then she remembered the vuvuzela."
    },
    {
      "id": "18",
      "text": "She tried to blow again."
    },
    {
      "id": "19",
      "text": "She blew very hard."
    },
    {
      "id": "20",
      "text": "A great sound came out!"
    },
    {
      "id": "21",
      "text": "Pbpbbrrrrwwwooo!"
    }
  ]
}
